'''''Asplenium ruta-muraria''''' is a species of [[fern]] commonly known as '''wall-rue'''<ref>{{Cite book|url=http://www.forest.go.kr/kna/special/download/English_Names_for_Korean_Native_Plants.pdf |title=English Names for Korean Native Plants |publisher=[[Korea National Arboretum]] |year=2015 |isbn=978-89-97450-98-5 |location=Pocheon |page=365 |access-date=25 January 2017 |via=[[Korea Forest Service]]  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170525105020/http://www.forest.go.kr/kna/special/download/English_Names_for_Korean_Native_Plants.pdf |archive-date=25 May 2017 }}</ref> (but which, as a fern, is not by any means closely related to common [[rue]]). It is a very small [[epipetric]] species, growing exclusively on [[limestone]] and other calcareous rocks. Its fronds are bluish-green and are heavily sub-divided, becoming up to {{Convert|12|cm|abbr=on}} in length. 
[[Image:Aspenium ruta-muraria2.JPG|left|thumb|Sori of ''A. ruta-muraria'']]

==Taxonomy==
[[Carl Linnaeus|Linnaeus]] first gave wall-rue the [[binomial nomenclature|binomial]] ''Asplenium ruta-muraria'' in his ''[[Species Plantarum]]'' of 1753.{{sfn|Linnaeus|1753|p=1081}} 

A global [[phylogeny]] of ''Asplenium'' published in 2020 divided the genus into eleven [[clade]]s,{{sfn|Xu|Zhang|Rothfels|Smith|2020|p=27}} which were given informal names pending further taxonomic study. ''A.&nbsp;ruta-muraria'' belongs to the "''Pleurosorus'' subclade" of the "''Pleurosorus'' clade".{{sfn|Xu|Zhang|Rothfels|Smith|2020|p=30}} The ''Pleurosorus'' clade has a worldwide distribution; members are generally small and occur on hillsides, often sheltering among rocks in exposed habitats. ''A.&nbsp;ruta-muraria'' is exceptional within the subclade for its lack of hairs on the leaf. The phylogeny suggests that multiple [[cryptic species]] may be present among plants now called ''A.&nbsp;ruta-muraria''.{{sfn|Xu|Zhang|Rothfels|Smith|2020|p=46}} Within the subclade, the ''A.&nbsp;ruta-muraria'' aggregate (including ''A.&nbsp;dolomiticum'') is [[Sister group|sister]] to the species formerly segregated in the genus ''Pleurosorus''.{{sfn|Xu|Zhang|Rothfels|Smith|2020|p=30}}

==Distribution and habitat==
''Asplenium ruta-muraria'' is native to Europe, East Asia, and eastern North America.{{sfn|Wagner|Moran|Werth|1993}} In North America, its range extends from western New England southwest along the [[Appalachian Mountains]] to Alabama and Tennessee. It is also found in the [[Ozarks]] and in southern Indiana and Ohio, with outlying occurrences in Michigan, Ontario, Quebec, and [[Clinton County, Iowa]].{{sfn|Kartesz|2014}} <!-- Flora of China discusses Eurasian distribution -->

In [[Europe]], it commonly invades masonry and is a common species, while in the [[United States]], it is more difficult to find, favouring pockets in very well-weathered and rather dry limestone outcrops. 

